window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-cb40e3ea80b9ead7"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"bring-your-app-to-chatgpt\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"chatgpt\">将你的应用接入 ChatGPT</h1> <p>把具体使用场景转化为专注、实用的 ChatGPT 应用。</p> <p>从头到尾构建一个范围明确的 ChatGPT 应用：定义工具、搭建 MCP 服务器和可选组件、在 ChatGPT 中连接，并通过迭代让核心流程正常运行。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>围绕一个用户目标规划第一个 ChatGPT 应用。</li> <li>搭建 MCP 服务器、工具元数据和可选组件，同时避免过度构建。</li> <li>通过本地 HTTPS 测试，逐步验证自定义 MCP 服务器是否能在 ChatGPT 中正常工作。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/chatgpt-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$chatgpt-apps（需联网）</a></td> <td>规划工具、连接 MCP 资源，并遵循当前 ChatGPT 应用构建流程。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/openai-docs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$openai-docs（需联网）</a></td> <td>在 Codex 编写代码或提出架构建议前，获取当前 OpenAI 官方 Apps SDK 指南。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/vercel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">vercel（需联网）</a></td> <td>在 Codex 中引入 Vercel 生态的使用指南和官方 Vercel MCP 服务器。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技术栈建议</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>需求</th> <th>建议选择</th> <th>原因</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>组件框架</td> <td><a href=\"https://react.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">React（需联网）</a></td> <td>对有状态组件而言是可靠的默认选择，尤其适合需要筛选器、表格或多步交互的界面。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>托管服务</td> <td><a href=\"https://vercel.com/docs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Vercel（需联网）</a></td> <td>可快速部署，提供预览环境和自动 HTTPS，并能方便地托管 MCP 端点。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>先规划应用，再搭建项目</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请在此代码库中使用 $chatgpt-apps 和 $openai-docs 为 [use case]（使用场景）规划一个 ChatGPT 应用。\n\n要求：\n- 从一个核心用户目标开始。\n- 提出 3–5 个工具，并清楚说明名称、描述、输入和输出。\n- 建议 v1 是否需要组件，还是可以先只提供数据。\n- MCP 服务器优先使用 TypeScript，组件优先使用 React。\n- 指明身份验证、部署和测试要求。\n\n输出：\n- 工具计划\n- 建议的文件树\n- 黄金提示词集合\n- 风险和待解决问题\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/plugins/quickstart\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Apps SDK 快速入门（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/plugins/build/mcp-server\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">构建 MCP 服务器（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/plugins/deploy/connect-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">测试（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"what-you-build\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">你将构建什么</h2> <p>每个由 MCP 提供支持的插件都由三部分组成：</p> <ul> <li>MCP 服务器：定义工具、返回数据、执行身份验证，并向 ChatGPT 提供 UI 资源的访问入口。</li> <li>可选的 Web 组件：在 ChatGPT iframe 中显示。你可以使用 React，也可以只用 HTML、CSS 和 JavaScript 构建。</li> <li>模型：根据你提供的元数据决定何时调用插件工具。</li> </ul> <p>Codex 最适合负责这些部分中重复性的工程工作：</p> <ul> <li>规划工具范围和元数据。</li> <li>搭建服务器和组件的初始结构。</li> <li>配置本地运行脚本。</li> <li>分阶段添加身份验证和部署相关改动。</li> <li>编写验证流程，确认插件能在 ChatGPT 中正常工作。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"why-codex-is-a-strong-fit\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">为什么适合使用 Codex</h2> <ul> <li>由 MCP 支持的插件可以清楚地拆分为服务器、可选 UI 和模型驱动的工具调用。</li> <li>Codex 在任务明确、范围有限且容易验证时效果更好，而这正适合插件开发。</li> <li>技能和 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 可以提供可复用的说明与项目规则，让 Codex 的工作始终有据可依。</li> </ul> <p>如需了解如何安装和使用技能，请参阅 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">技能文档（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"how-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">使用方法</h2> <p><a id=\"prerequisites\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">前置条件</h2> <ul> <li>先确定一个核心用户目标，不要试图把整个产品都迁移到聊天界面。</li> <li>提前选好技术栈：服务器使用 TypeScript 或 Python；组件使用 React，或采用轻量的 HTML、CSS 和 JavaScript。</li> <li>确定开发时使用哪种 HTTPS 通道，例如 <code>ngrok</code> 或 Cloudflare Tunnel。</li> <li> <p>有些设置中仍保留了旧的 MCP 服务器连接术语。在本地测试时，可以将这些标签理解为已注册的服务器。</p> </li> <li> <p>从一个范围明确的插件目标开始，让 Codex 提出 3–5 个工具，并清楚说明各自的名称、描述、输入和输出。</p> </li> <li>判断 v1 是否可以只提供数据，还是需要组件；随后先复用代码库现有模式，再搭建 MCP 服务器和可选组件，最后才添加依赖。</li> <li>在本地通过 HTTPS 运行 MCP 服务器，在 ChatGPT 中使用<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/custom-mcp-server.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">添加自定义 MCP 服务器</a>进行连接，并用少量直接、间接和负向提示词进行测试。</li> <li>逐步调整元数据、状态处理、<code>structuredContent</code> 和 <code>_meta</code> 载荷，直到核心读取流程在 ChatGPT 中稳定运行。</li> <li>只有在确实需要访问用户专属数据或执行写入操作时，才添加 OAuth 2.1；不要让匿名或只读流程变复杂。</li> <li>准备一个具有稳定 <code>/mcp</code> 端点的托管预览，验证流式传输和 UI 素材托管，并在分享或提交插件前检查发布准备清单。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"suggested-prompts\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">建议的提示词</h2> <p>适用于此工作流程的提示词通常包含以下要素：</p> <ul> <li>一个明确目标：说明插件要帮助用户在 ChatGPT 中完成什么。</li> <li>明确的技术栈：说明服务器使用 TypeScript 还是 Python；组件使用 React 还是轻量实现。</li> <li>明确的工具边界：请 Codex 提出或构建一小组工具，每个工具只承担一项职责。</li> <li>身份验证要求：说明初版是否可匿名使用，还是需要关联账户和写入操作。</li> <li>本地开发路径：说明你计划使用哪种隧道或托管方式，在 ChatGPT 中进行 HTTPS 测试。</li> <li>验证步骤：说明要运行哪些命令、测试哪些提示词，以及需要报告哪些证据。</li> </ul> <p>不要用一个超长提示词同时要求规划、实现、身份验证、部署、提交和润色。应把工作拆分为更小的里程碑。</p> <p><strong>在搭建项目前先规划插件</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $chatgpt-apps with $openai-docs to plan an MCP-backed plugin for [use case] in this repo.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Start with one core user outcome.\n- Propose 3-5 tools with clear names, descriptions, inputs, and outputs.\n- Recommend whether v1 needs a widget or can start data-only.\n- Prefer TypeScript for the MCP server and React for the widget.\n- Call out auth, deployment, and test requirements.\n\nOutput:\n\n- Tool plan\n- Proposed file tree\n- Golden prompt set\n- Risks and open questions\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">结合使用 $chatgpt-apps 和 $openai-docs，在这个仓库中为 [use case] 规划一个由 MCP 提供支持的插件。\n\n要求：\n\n- 从一个核心用户目标开始。\n- 提出 3-5 个工具，并清楚说明其名称、描述、输入和输出。\n- 建议 v1 是否需要小组件，或是否可以先只提供数据。\n- MCP 服务器优先使用 TypeScript，小组件优先使用 React。\n- 明确说明身份验证、部署和测试要求。\n\n输出：\n\n- 工具方案\n- 建议的文件目录树\n- 基准提示词集\n- 风险和待解决的问题</div></div> <p><strong>搭建第一个可运行版本</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $chatgpt-apps with $openai-docs to scaffold the first version of this MCP-backed plugin.\n\nStack:\n\n- TypeScript MCP server\n- React widget\n- Vite build\n- Local HTTPS via ngrok\n\nConstraints:\n\n- Keep the plugin narrow: one read flow and at most one write flow.\n- Return concise structuredContent for the model and reserve widget-only data for \\_meta.\n- Make tool handlers idempotent.\n- Reuse existing repo patterns before adding dependencies.\n\nVerification:\n\n- Start the local server\n- Explain how to connect the MCP server in ChatGPT using Add custom MCP server\n- List the exact prompts to test\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">结合使用 $chatgpt-apps 和 $openai-docs，搭建这个由 MCP 提供支持的插件的第一版框架。\n\n技术栈：\n\n- TypeScript MCP 服务器\n- React 小组件\n- Vite 构建\n- 通过 ngrok 提供本地 HTTPS\n\n约束：\n\n- 缩小插件范围：只包含一条读取流程，以及至多一条写入流程。\n- 为模型返回简洁的 structuredContent，将仅供小组件使用的数据放在 \\_meta 中。\n- 让工具处理程序具有幂等性。\n- 添加依赖项前，先复用仓库中已有的实现模式。\n\n验证：\n\n- 启动本地服务器。\n- 说明如何在 ChatGPT 中通过 Add custom MCP server（添加自定义 MCP 服务器）连接该 MCP 服务器。\n- 列出用于测试的确切提示词。</div></div> <p><strong>核心流程正常后再添加身份验证</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $chatgpt-apps with $openai-docs to add auth to this plugin's MCP server.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Keep read-only tools anonymous if possible.\n- Add OAuth 2.1 only for user-specific data or write actions.\n- Use an existing identity provider such as Auth0 or Stytch.\n- Document scopes, token checks, and the custom MCP server test flow in ChatGPT.\n\nOutput:\n\n- Auth flow summary\n- Server changes\n- Required environment variables\n- End-to-end test plan\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">结合使用 $chatgpt-apps 和 $openai-docs，为这个插件的 MCP 服务器添加身份验证。\n\n要求：\n\n- 如果可行，让只读工具继续支持匿名访问。\n- 仅对用户专属数据或写入操作添加 OAuth 2.1。\n- 使用 Auth0 或 Stytch 等现有身份提供方。\n- 记录权限范围、令牌检查，以及在 ChatGPT 中测试自定义 MCP 服务器的流程。\n\n输出：\n\n- 身份验证流程概要\n- 服务器变更\n- 必需的环境变量\n- 端到端测试计划</div></div> <p><strong>准备部署并接受审查</strong></p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $chatgpt-apps with $openai-docs and @vercel to prepare this plugin for a hosted preview.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Expose a stable HTTPS /mcp endpoint.\n- Keep streaming responses working on /mcp.\n- Host widget assets correctly.\n- Add a launch-readiness checklist covering metadata, tool hints, privacy, and test prompts.\n\nOutput:\n\n- Deployment plan\n- Preview URL or hosting steps\n- Review checklist\n- Remaining risks\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">结合使用 $chatgpt-apps、$openai-docs 和 @vercel，为这个插件准备托管预览。\n\n要求：\n\n- 提供稳定的 HTTPS /mcp 端点。\n- 确保 /mcp 上的流式响应正常工作。\n- 正确托管小组件资源。\n- 添加上线准备检查清单，涵盖元数据、工具提示信息、隐私和测试提示词。\n\n输出：\n\n- 部署计划\n- 预览 URL 或托管步骤\n- 审查清单\n- 剩余风险</div></div> <p><a id=\"launch-readiness\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">发布准备情况</h2> <ul> <li>插件只有一个范围明确、用户容易理解的目标。</li> <li>工具数量保持精简，并且具有明确的元数据、输入和输出。</li> <li>MCP 服务器可以端到端正常工作，返回简洁的 <code>structuredContent</code>，并将仅供组件使用的数据保留在 <code>_meta</code> 中。</li> <li>如果需要组件，它能在 ChatGPT 中正确显示。</li> <li>已建立本地 HTTPS 测试流程，并能在 ChatGPT 中连接自定义 MCP 服务器。</li> <li>少量直接、间接和负向提示词测试均符合预期的对话流程和工具载荷。</li> <li>只有用户专属数据或写入操作确实需要时，才添加身份验证。</li> <li>分享或提交插件前，部署计划和发布准备审查已涵盖元数据、工具提示、隐私和测试提示词。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"common-pitfalls\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">常见问题</h2> <ul> <li><strong>要求 Codex 将整个产品迁移到 ChatGPT。</strong>更合适的做法：先确定一个核心用户目标、三到五个工具和一个范围明确的组件。</li> <li><strong>一开始就提供超长的实现提示词。</strong>更合适的做法：把工作拆成规划、搭建、身份验证、部署和审查几个阶段。</li> <li><strong>工具约定尚未明确，就先开始编写 UI。</strong>更合适的做法：先规划工具范围和响应结构，再构建组件。</li> <li><strong>没有依据官方文档来约束实现。</strong>更合适的做法：同时使用 <code>$chatgpt-apps</code> 和 <code>$openai-docs</code>，让初始搭建过程遵循当前插件指南。</li> <li><strong>把元数据当作次要工作。</strong>更合适的做法：尽早编写工具说明和参数文档，再用一组提示词反复测试。</li> <li><strong>核心流程还没验证就先添加身份验证。</strong>更合适的做法：先跑通匿名或只读流程，再为确有需要的工具添加 OAuth。</li> <li><strong>没有在 ChatGPT 中实测，就宣称插件已完成。</strong>更合适的做法：连接自定义 MCP 服务器，检查工具载荷，并验证真实对话流程。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"bring-your-app-to-chatgpt\">Bring your app to ChatGPT</h1> <p>Turn your use cases into focused apps for ChatGPT.</p> <p>Build one narrow ChatGPT app outcome end to end: define the tools, scaffold the MCP server and optional widget, connect it in ChatGPT, and iterate until the core flow works.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Planning a first ChatGPT app around a user outcome</li> <li>Scaffolding an MCP server, tool metadata, and an optional widget without overbuilding</li> <li>Running a tight loop from local HTTPS testing to custom MCP server verification in ChatGPT</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/chatgpt-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$chatgpt-apps (online)</a></td> <td>Plan tools, wire MCP resources, and follow the current ChatGPT app build flow.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.curated/openai-docs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$openai-docs (online)</a></td> <td>Pull current official Apps SDK guidance before Codex writes code or suggests architecture.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/vercel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">vercel (online)</a></td> <td>Bring Vercel ecosystem guidance into Codex with curated skills and the official Vercel MCP server.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\">Tech stack recommendations</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Need</th> <th>Good default</th> <th>Why</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Widget framework</td> <td><a href=\"https://react.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">React (online)</a></td> <td>A strong default for stateful widgets, especially when the UI needs filters, tables, or multi-step interaction.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Hosting</td> <td><a href=\"https://vercel.com/docs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Vercel (online)</a></td> <td>Quick deploys, preview environments, automatic HTTPS, and a clear path to hosted MCP endpoints.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Plan the App Before You Scaffold It</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $chatgpt-apps with $openai-docs to plan a ChatGPT app for [use case] in this repo.\n\nRequirements:\n- Start with one core user outcome.\n- Propose 3-5 tools with clear names, descriptions, inputs, and outputs.\n- Recommend whether v1 needs a widget or can start data-only.\n- Prefer TypeScript for the MCP server and React for the widget.\n- Call out auth, deployment, and test requirements.\n\nOutput:\n- Tool plan\n- Proposed file tree\n- Golden prompt set\n- Risks and open questions\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/plugins/quickstart\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Apps SDK quickstart (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/plugins/build/mcp-server\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build an MCP server (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/plugins/deploy/connect-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Testing (online)</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"what-you-build\">What you build</h2> <p>Every MCP-backed plugin has three parts:</p> <ul> <li>An MCP server that defines tools, returns data, enforces auth, and points ChatGPT at any UI resources.</li> <li>An optional web component that renders inside a ChatGPT iframe. You can build it with React or with plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.</li> <li>A model that decides when to call the plugin's tools based on the metadata you provide.</li> </ul> <p>Codex is most useful when it owns the repetitive engineering work around those parts:</p> <ul> <li>Planning the tool surface and metadata.</li> <li>Scaffolding the server and widget.</li> <li>Wiring local run scripts.</li> <li>Adding auth and deployment changes in focused passes.</li> <li>Writing the verification loop that proves the plugin works in ChatGPT.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"why-codex-is-a-strong-fit\">Why Codex is a strong fit</h2> <ul> <li>MCP-backed plugins split cleanly into a server, optional UI, and model-driven tool calls.</li> <li>Codex prompting works best when the task is explicit, scoped, and straightforward to verify, which matches plugin-building work well.</li> <li>Skills and <code>AGENTS.md</code> give Codex the reusable instructions and project rules it needs to stay grounded.</li> </ul> <p>To learn more about how to install and use skills, see our <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">skills documentation (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"how-to-use\">How to use</h2> <h2 id=\"prerequisites\">Prerequisites</h2> <ul> <li>Start with one core user outcome instead of trying to port an entire product into chat.</li> <li>Choose the stack up front: TypeScript or Python for the server, and React or plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript for the widget.</li> <li>Decide what HTTPS path you will use during development, such as <code>ngrok</code> or Cloudflare Tunnel.</li> <li> <p>Some settings still use older terms for an MCP server connection. During local testing, treat those labels as referring to the registered server.</p> </li> <li> <p>Start with one narrow plugin outcome and ask Codex to propose three to five tools with clear names, descriptions, inputs, and outputs.</p> </li> <li>Decide whether v1 can stay data-only or needs a widget, then scaffold the MCP server and optional widget using existing repository patterns before adding dependencies.</li> <li>Run the MCP server locally behind HTTPS, connect it in ChatGPT with <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/custom-mcp-server.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add custom MCP server</a>, and test it with a small direct, indirect, and negative prompt set.</li> <li>Iterate on metadata, state handling, <code>structuredContent</code>, and <code>_meta</code> payloads until the core read flow behaves reliably inside ChatGPT.</li> <li>Add OAuth 2.1 only when user-specific data or write actions require it, without complicating anonymous or read-only flows.</li> <li>Prepare a hosted preview with a stable <code>/mcp</code> endpoint, verify streaming and UI asset hosting, and review the launch checklist before sharing or submitting the plugin.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"suggested-prompts\">Suggested prompts</h2> <p>Strong prompts for this workflow share the same ingredients:</p> <ul> <li>One clear outcome: say what the plugin should help the user do inside ChatGPT.</li> <li>A concrete stack: say whether you want TypeScript or Python on the server, and whether the widget should use React or stay lightweight.</li> <li>Explicit tool boundaries: ask Codex to propose or build a small set of tools with one job per tool.</li> <li>Auth expectations: state whether the first version can be anonymous or whether it needs linked accounts and write actions.</li> <li>A local development path: mention the tunnel or hosting path you expect for HTTPS testing in ChatGPT.</li> <li>Verification steps: tell Codex what commands to run, what prompts to test, and what evidence to report back.</li> </ul> <p>Avoid one giant prompt that asks for planning, implementation, auth, deployment, submission, and polish in one pass. Split the work into smaller milestones instead.</p> <p><strong>Plan the Plugin Before You Scaffold It</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $chatgpt-apps with $openai-docs to plan an MCP-backed plugin for [use case] in this repo.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Start with one core user outcome.\n- Propose 3-5 tools with clear names, descriptions, inputs, and outputs.\n- Recommend whether v1 needs a widget or can start data-only.\n- Prefer TypeScript for the MCP server and React for the widget.\n- Call out auth, deployment, and test requirements.\n\nOutput:\n\n- Tool plan\n- Proposed file tree\n- Golden prompt set\n- Risks and open questions\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Scaffold the First Working Version</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $chatgpt-apps with $openai-docs to scaffold the first version of this MCP-backed plugin.\n\nStack:\n\n- TypeScript MCP server\n- React widget\n- Vite build\n- Local HTTPS via ngrok\n\nConstraints:\n\n- Keep the plugin narrow: one read flow and at most one write flow.\n- Return concise structuredContent for the model and reserve widget-only data for \\_meta.\n- Make tool handlers idempotent.\n- Reuse existing repo patterns before adding dependencies.\n\nVerification:\n\n- Start the local server\n- Explain how to connect the MCP server in ChatGPT using Add custom MCP server\n- List the exact prompts to test\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Add Auth Only After the Core Flow Works</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $chatgpt-apps with $openai-docs to add auth to this plugin's MCP server.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Keep read-only tools anonymous if possible.\n- Add OAuth 2.1 only for user-specific data or write actions.\n- Use an existing identity provider such as Auth0 or Stytch.\n- Document scopes, token checks, and the custom MCP server test flow in ChatGPT.\n\nOutput:\n\n- Auth flow summary\n- Server changes\n- Required environment variables\n- End-to-end test plan\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Prepare the Plugin for Deployment and Review</strong></p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $chatgpt-apps with $openai-docs and @vercel to prepare this plugin for a hosted preview.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Expose a stable HTTPS /mcp endpoint.\n- Keep streaming responses working on /mcp.\n- Host widget assets correctly.\n- Add a launch-readiness checklist covering metadata, tool hints, privacy, and test prompts.\n\nOutput:\n\n- Deployment plan\n- Preview URL or hosting steps\n- Review checklist\n- Remaining risks\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"launch-readiness\">Launch readiness</h2> <ul> <li>The plugin has one narrow outcome that users can understand.</li> <li>The tool set stays small and has explicit metadata, inputs, and outputs.</li> <li>The MCP server works end to end and returns concise <code>structuredContent</code>, reserving widget-only data for <code>_meta</code>.</li> <li>The widget, if needed, renders correctly inside ChatGPT.</li> <li>A local HTTPS testing loop works with the custom MCP server connected in ChatGPT.</li> <li>A small direct, indirect, and negative prompt set passes with the expected conversation flow and tool payloads.</li> <li>Auth is added only where user-specific data or write actions require it.</li> <li>A deployment plan and launch-readiness review cover metadata, tool hints, privacy, and test prompts before the plugin is shared or submitted.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"common-pitfalls\">Common pitfalls</h2> <ul> <li>Asking Codex to port the whole product into ChatGPT. Better move: ask for one core user outcome, three to five tools, and one narrow widget.</li> <li>Starting with a giant implementation prompt. Better move: split the work into planning, scaffold, auth, deployment, and review passes.</li> <li>Writing UI before the tool contract is clear. Better move: plan the tool surface and response schema first, then build the widget.</li> <li>Skipping official docs grounding. Better move: pair <code>$chatgpt-apps</code> with <code>$openai-docs</code> so the scaffold follows current plugin guidance.</li> <li>Treating metadata as an afterthought. Better move: write tool descriptions and parameter docs early, then replay a prompt set against them.</li> <li>Adding auth before proving the anonymous or read-only path. Better move: get the core tool flow working first, then add OAuth for the tools that actually need it.</li> <li>Declaring the plugin done before testing inside ChatGPT. Better move: connect the custom MCP server in ChatGPT, inspect tool payloads, and verify the real conversation flow.</li> </ul>"};
